    "body": "Help me understand. Are you saying you don't want to update this [Events non-normative table](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#events-2) because the [UI Events spec for `beforeinput`](https://www.w3.org/TR/uievents/#event-type-beforeinput) isn't well maintained? It looks like all events described in UI Events are hard-coded with fixed sync/bubbles/cancelable/etc properties. Is it just that you think `beforeinput` is special there? Perhaps you're saying we shouldn't link to the definition in UI Events at all, and define it here instead?\r\n\r\nI guess: please tell me specifically what you'd like me to change here, and I'll change it.",
